#: ../../reference/asm_thumb2_ldr.rst:2
msgid "Load register from memory"
msgstr "从内存加载寄存器"

#: ../../reference/asm_thumb2_ldr.rst:5
msgid "Document conventions"
msgstr "文档约定"

#: ../../reference/asm_thumb2_ldr.rst:7
msgid ""
"Notation: ``Rt, Rn`` denote ARM registers R0-R7 except where stated. "
"``immN`` represents an immediate value having a width of N bits hence "
"``imm5`` is constrained to the range 0-31. ``[Rn + immN]`` is the contents "
"of the memory address obtained by adding Rn and the offset ``immN``. Offsets"
" are measured in bytes. These instructions affect the condition flags."
msgstr ""
"记法：\\ ``Rt, Rn`` 除非另有说明，表示 ARM 寄存器 R0-R7。\\ ``immN`` 表示位宽为 N 位的立即数，因此 "
"``imm5`` 被约束在 0-31 范围内。\\ ``[Rn + immN]`` 是将 Rn 与偏移量 ``immN`` "
"相加所得内存地址处的内容。偏移量以字节为单位。这些指令会影响条件标志。"

#: ../../reference/asm_thumb2_ldr.rst:13
msgid "Register Load"
msgstr "寄存器加载"

#: ../../reference/asm_thumb2_ldr.rst:15
msgid "ldr(Rt, [Rn, imm7]) ``Rt = [Rn + imm7]`` Load a 32 bit word"
msgstr "ldr(Rt, [Rn, imm7]) ``Rt = [Rn + imm7]`` 加载一个 32 位字"

#: ../../reference/asm_thumb2_ldr.rst:16
msgid "ldrb(Rt, [Rn, imm5]) ``Rt = [Rn + imm5]`` Load a byte"
msgstr "ldrb(Rt, [Rn, imm5]) ``Rt = [Rn + imm5]`` 加载一个字节"

#: ../../reference/asm_thumb2_ldr.rst:17
msgid "ldrh(Rt, [Rn, imm6]) ``Rt = [Rn + imm6]`` Load a 16 bit half word"
msgstr "ldrh(Rt, [Rn, imm6]) ``Rt = [Rn + imm6]`` 加载一个 16 位半字"

#: ../../reference/asm_thumb2_ldr.rst:19
msgid "Where a byte or half word is loaded, it is zero-extended to 32 bits."
msgstr "在加载字节或半字时，它会被零扩展到 32 位。"

#: ../../reference/asm_thumb2_ldr.rst:21
msgid ""
"The specified immediate offsets are measured in bytes. Hence in the case of "
"``ldr`` the 7 bit value enables 32 bit word aligned values to be accessed "
"with a maximum offset of 31 words. In the case of ``ldrh`` the 6 bit value "
"enables 16 bit half-word aligned values to be accessed with a maximum offset"
" of 31 half-words."
msgstr ""
"所指定的立即偏移量以字节为单位。因此对于 ``ldr``\\ ，7 位的值使得可以以最大 31 个字的偏移量访问 32 位字对齐的值。对于 "
"``ldrh``\\ ，6 位的值使得可以以最大 31 个半字的偏移量访问 16 位半字对齐的值。"
